linux-rockchip64-ysp (6.18.38+rk3588av1fwport20260724-0ubuntu1~rk1) resolute; urgency=high

  * RGA3 10-bit stride ABI fix (regression): the legacy RGA_BLIT ABI carries
    10-bit vir_w as a byte stride (the BSP contract the RGA2 writer honors),
    but the RGA3 raster writer had been scaling it by pixel depth (x10/8 or
    x2), over-reading every legacy 10-bit raster and faulting the RGA3 IOMMU.
    Program all three RGA3 raster windows byte-literally and teach the
    stride-align check that a 10-bit stride unit is a byte. Surfaced by the
    JeffyCN GStreamer H.265 Main10 -> RGA-scale path; pairs with the librga
    im2d pixel->byte conversion. Fixes the interim byte-literal-stride change
    shipped in 20260723.
  * RGA2 MMU page tables fail closed on above-4G entries: reject a userptr
    whose page address would truncate past 32 bits (-EOPNOTSUPP) instead of
    programming a wrong page and hitting an RGA2 hardware bus error.

 -- Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>  Thu, 24 Jul 2026 07:00:00 -0700

linux-rockchip64-ysp (6.18.38+rk3588av1fwport20260723-0ubuntu1~rk1) resolute; urgency=high

  * RGA legacy-ABI compatibility: accept the legacy RGA2_GET_RESULT no-op and
    the historical virtual-address blit convention; validate staged
    REQUEST_CONFIG task lists and report the RGA2 under-4G exclusion distinctly.
  * RGA 10-bit correctness: program byte-literal WIN/WR strides and derive UV
    plane offsets byte-literally for P010/P210/NV15, fixing the stock-vendor
    10-bit corruption.
  * RGA2 DMA integrity: own the MMU page tables through the DMA API and serve
    over-4G memory via a swiotlb-bounced mapping instead of an illegal
    virt_to_phys() streaming sync.
  * Memory-safety fixes on driver code shared with the Rockchip BSP: drop an RGA
    request's initial reference exactly once (UAF/refcount underflow); hold a
    session reference for a job's lifetime (IRQ-thread UAF); guard the MPP async
    worker and wait/poll paths against a device-less orphan task (NULL-deref
    hard lockup); bounds-check register-translation imports (OOB writes); unmap
    the RCB IOVA before freeing its pages; and reject RELEASE_FD on a session
    with no DMA context.
  * BSP-audit HIGH port: validate session fds before switching (type confusion),
    bound RCB/class register indexes, test each core's own disable flag, balance
    acquire-fence references, clean shutdown jobs outside the IRQ lock
    (sleep-in-atomic), validate multi-plane handles, make get-buffer error
    ownership symmetric, unwind partial handle acquisition, and require the core
    feature mask to be a superset of the request.
  * MPP: reject a second INIT_CLIENT_TYPE on an already-bound session with
    -EBUSY, closing an unprivileged double-init use-after-free.
  * RGA: do not drop mm->lock during session-release teardown (forward-port
    regression fix); reject a non-16-byte-aligned RGA3 IOMMU window base with
    -EINVAL instead of silently returning all-zero pixels.

 -- Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>  Thu, 23 Jul 2026 20:05:15 -0700

